  {
    "_ulid": "01KGVGY4W7WW86TVVR6HB1YX3H",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Support ephemeral workflow runs without persistent state",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "Ephemeral workflow runs - Add support for workflows that don't persist run state. Use cases: simple instruction flows, quick checklists, trivial step sequences. Options: (1) --ephemeral flag on 'workflow start', (2) workflow.ephemeral field in definition, (3) both with override. Ephemeral runs: no file storage, no shadow commits, not shown in 'workflow runs', state only in session context or just sequential display. Reduces noise for simple flows.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "status": "pending",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [
      "workflow",
      "dx"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-07T07:44:20.870Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGVGY4W7Z0QCMW9Y1RT6QJCN",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T07:44:20.871Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation: Needs spec/design first. Core question: how does step tracking work without a run file? Options: (1) ephemeral field on workflow definition in meta YAML, (2) --ephemeral flag on workflow start, (3) both with override. Execution model: write run file to temp location (not .kspec/), auto-delete on completion. workflow next/show still work via temp file. No shadow commits during run. Not shown in workflow runs. This avoids rethinking the execution model while achieving the goal of no persistent noise. Affects: workflow start, next, show, runs commands.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGVJKZWYET14PKPZXRZG1RW4",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T08:13:45.246Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Automation status set to needs_review: Fundamental workflow execution model change needs design",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHD9G0KEHAV8GARY598JX6GW",
        "created_at": "2026-02-14T05:20:37.486Z",
        "author": "@claude",
